 practice combined with physical practice for upper-limb motor deficit in subacute stroke</article-title><source>Phys Ther</source><year>2001</year><volume>81</volume><fpage>1455</fpage><lpage>1462</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11509075</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Higgins</surname><given-names>JPTGS</given-names></name><collab>editors</collab></person-group><article-title>Cochrane Handbook for Systematic Reviews of Interventions 4.2.6 (updated September 2006)</article-title><source>The Cochrane Library</source><year>2006</year><publisher-name>Chichester, UK: John Wiley &#x00026; Sons, Ltd</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>KP</given-names></name><name><surname>Chan</surname><given-names>CC</given-names></name><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>TM</given-names></name><name><surname>Hui-Chan</surname><given-names>CW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mental imagery for promoting relearning for people after stroke: a randomized controlled trial</article-title><source>Archives of Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation</source><year>2004</year><volume>85</volume><fpage>1403</fpage><lpage>1408</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15375808</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.apmr.2003.12.035</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Page</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effects of Mental Practice on Affected Limb Use and Function in Chronic Stroke</article-title><source>Arch Phys Med Rehabil</source><year>2005</year><volume>86</volume><fpage>399</fpage><lpage>402</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15759218</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.apmr.2004.10.002</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id=